In the `PUT_LastIndexOfContract` test case, the assertion checks if the newly returned value is greater than or equal to the old index value, ensuring that if the return value is positive (meaning that it was found in the old list), it is indeed at least the index of `x` in the old list.--------------------Here's how you can extract the comment lines that start with "@@@" into assert statements:

```cs
Debug.Assert(New_arrListCount > Old_arrListCount); 
Debug.Assert(Old_arrListIndexOfX == -1 || Old_arrListIndexOfX == New_arrListIndexOfX); 
Debug.Assert(Old_arrListLastIndexOfX == -1 || Old_arrListLastIndexOfX == New_arrListLastIndexOfX); 

Debug.Assert(New_arrListContainsX == New_Ret == New_arrListIndexOfX != -1); 
Debug.Assert(New_arrListContainsX == (Old_arrListIndexOfX == -1 || Old_arrListIndexOfX != New_arrListIndexOfX)); 

